      "pinNotes": [
        {
          "at": "2026-10-12",
          "note": "Two drifts repaired. The pin was moved to pack commit c3c542d on 2026-10-10 without updating pack.json's digest (325d6ee477f9 -> f6834e6cb2c7) or the acquisition stage word, and the pack commit had never been pushed, so validate:packs answered HTTP 404 rather than reporting either. Pushing the pack made both visible.\n\nThe stage word is the pack's, not a guess: its manifest declares acquisition 'out-of-scope' with the measurement behind it -- Zenodo serves the record with access-control-allow-origin: * and honours Range requests, answering 206 with a Content-Range -- and its own commit is titled 'Acquisition is out of scope by decision, not impossible in a browser'. The host said 'excluded', which was the older and weaker claim."
        },
        "Repository archived on GitHub 2026-10-26. An archived repository stays publicly readable, so the pinned commit still resolves -- verified at HTTP 200 -- and both the clone and the network fallback keep working. Archiving removes the invitation to push, not the ability to read."
